  "cil_liability": null,
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The proposal, by reason of the insufficient proportion of\r\nfamily-sized homes with three or more bedrooms and its preponderance of smaller\r\nstudio and 1-bed units, would fail to achieve an appropriate housing mix,\r\nhaving regard to the location of the site and its surroundings as well as the\r\nevidence of local need which identifies the need for more larger, family-sized\r\nunits and would fail to contribute to the creation of inclusive and mixed\r\ncommunities, contrary to the provisions of NDMP HO7 of the National Planning\r\nPolicy Framework (2026), Policies H1, H2 and H10 of the London Plan (2021) and\r\nPolicy HO1.A.1 of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoListParagraph&quot; style=&quot;text-align: justify;&quot;&gt;The proposed development, by reason of the proposed\r\nsubdivision of the rear garden into five separate amenity spaces would, taking\r\ninto account the size of the plot, result in a form of development which would\r\nbe at odds with the prevailing character and appearance and spatial grain of\r\nthe area. The subdivision would erode the spaciousness and verdant quality of\r\nthe plot and the plethora of boundary fencing would create an awkward\r\ncompartmentalisation and fragmentation of the garden, resulting in cramped,\r\ncontrived, poor amenity areas for future occupiers.&amp;nbsp; The proposed development is contrary to\r\nPolicies GR1 and HO2(g) of the Harrow Local Plan (2021-2041).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ]
}